# 7. `&&` and `||`

### AND – `&&`

Run the second command only if the first succeeds.

```bash
mkdir /tmp/test && echo "Directory created"
```

### OR – `||`

Run the second command if the first fails.

```bash
mkdir /tmp/test || echo "Directory creation failed"
```

### Combine them

```bash
mkdir /tmp/devops && echo "Success" || echo "Failed"
```

